hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1200","Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub Al-Jazari told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the Banu Abd al-Ashhal and led the Maghrib prayer with them. When he greeted him, he said: “Kneel down with these two The two rak'ahs in your homes. He said: “I saw Mahmoud, who was the imam of his people, leading them in the Maghrib prayer, then he went out and sat in the courtyard of the mosque until he got up shortly before Darkness, then he enters the house and leads them in prayer.”"
"1201","Bundar told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Wazir told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Fitri told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b bin Ujrah, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed the Maghrib prayer in the Bani Abd al-Ashhal Mosque. When he prayed, people got up to perform voluntary prayers. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You must perform this prayer in your homes.”"
